-- title:
--   Units lift along S → S/𝔪_R S for integral algebras
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ and $S$ be commutative rings with $S$ an $R$-algebra, let $R$ be local with maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}_R =$ `IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R`, and assume $S$ is integral over $R$ (every element of $S$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $R$, the typeclass `Algebra.IsIntegral R S`). Let $a \in S$, and let $\mathfrak{m}_R S$ denote the ideal of $S$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak{m}_R$ under the structure map $R \to S$, i.e. `(IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R).map (algebraMap R S)`. The hypothesis is that the residue class of $a$ under the quotient map $S \to S/\mathfrak{m}_R S$ is a unit of $S/\mathfrak{m}_R S$. The conclusion is that $a$ is itself a unit of $S$. Thus units reflect along the quotient $S \to S/\mathfrak{m}_R S$ when $S$ is integral over the local ring $R$.
--
--   This is the standard statement that, for $S$ integral over a local ring $R$, the ideal $\mathfrak{m}_R S$ is contained in the Jacobson radical of $S$, so that $S \to S/\mathfrak{m}_R S$ detects units. It is used in the local-algebra input to the deformation-theoretic part of the argument, via the statement [`HopfAlgebra.point_eq_one_of_forall_mem_inertiaSubgroupIn_eq_pow_of_isLocalRing_cartierDual_padicInt`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.point_eq_one_of_forall_mem_inertiaSubgroupIn_eq_pow_of_isLocalRing_cartierDual_padicInt).
